     2	\label{sec:related}
     3	
     4	\paragraph{Model Collapse Theory.}
     5	\citet{shumailov2024_nature} demonstrate that recursive training on model outputs erodes distributional tails; \citet{dohmatob2024_tale_of_tails} formalize this via scaling laws \cite{seddik2024synthetic}, \citet{dohmatob2025_strong_collapse} establish strong collapse guarantees, and the MAD framework \cite{alemohammad2024_mad} extends the analysis to self-consuming models.
     6	Subsequent work addresses mitigation \cite{gerstgrasser2024_accumulate,drayson2025_detection_prevents_collapse,yi2026_escaping_collapse,falahati2026_curated}, non-monotonic dynamics \cite{bakshi2026_collapse_improvement}, convergence \cite{marchi2024_heat_death,wang2026_contamination,knowledge_collapse2025,dohmatob2024_demystified}, and diversity decline \cite{guo2024curious,briesch2024selfconsuming,padmakumar2024diversity,sigma2026_spectral,synthetic_eggs2026}.
     7	All assume depth is known a priori; we address the inverse problem of estimating depth from text alone.
     8	
     9	\paragraph{AI Text Detection.}
    10	The detection literature \cite{wu2025_detection_survey} spans statistical methods---DetectGPT \cite{mitchell2023_detectgpt}, Fast-DetectGPT \cite{fast_detectgpt2024}, Binoculars \cite{binoculars2024}, DivEye \cite{diveye2026}, GLTR \cite{gehrmann2019_gltr}, Ghostbuster \cite{verma2024_ghostbuster}, DNA-GPT \cite{yang2024_dnagpt}---and watermarking \cite{kirchenbauer2023_watermark}, with known limits from paraphrasing \cite{sadasivan2023_paraphrase}, distribution shift \cite{pudasaini2026_detection_fails}, and generator barriers \cite{pu2026_generator_barrier}.
    11	These methods perform binary classification, discarding ordinal depth information; our approach outputs ordinal depth labels, complementing binary detection.
    12	
    13	\paragraph{Adjacent Tasks.}
    14	EditLens \cite{editlens2026} estimates editing extent but does not model recursive chains; \citet{uchendu2020_attribution} classify \emph{which} model generated text; LOKI \cite{loki2025} benchmarks synthetic data detection across modalities.
    15	\citet{mohamed2025_broken_telephone} study iterative generation as a ``broken telephone'' without classifying iteration depth; self-play methods like SPIN \cite{chen2024spin} instead exploit iterative training for improvement.
    16	Our task inverts the problem---estimating ordinal depth from text alone, discriminating adjacent depths rather than detecting aggregate degradation.
    17	
    18	\paragraph{Ordinal Classification.}
    19	CORAL \cite{coral2020} enforces rank consistency via ordered binary tasks; CLOC \cite{cloc2025} extends contrastive learning with multi-margin ordinal losses.
    20	We adopt both as baselines (\S\ref{sec:generalization}) to confirm the signal is accessible to principled ordinal methods.
    21	
    22	\paragraph{Decoding Strategy Effects.}
    23	Decoding strategies shape text statistics in ways that interact with depth signals \cite{holtzman2020_nucleus,finlayson2024_closing,garces_arias2025_decoding_decoded,wiher2022_decoding,basu2021_mirostat}.
    24	Our Depth Degradation Atlas (\S\ref{sec:atlas}) reveals qualitatively different degradation trajectories---temperature sampling accelerates convergence to a low-entropy attractor while top-$k$ attenuates the depth signal---effects beyond single-pass text quality.
